	(footprint "MiniDIN6_PS2_Socket_CUI_MD-60S"
		(layer "F.Cu")
		(uuid "c5ef4afa-f5e4-461d-9e79-bd35fe4c06ec")
		(at 72 -2.25)
		(descr "Mini-DIN 6-pin (PS/2) female PCB socket, right-angle THT, Same Sky / CUI Devices MD-60S; hole grid also matches Kycon KMDGX-6S. Amiga A4000 keyboard connector, which uses the PS/2 pin positions exactly: 1=KDAT 3=GND 4=+5V 5=KCLK, 2 and 6 NC. Dimensions from the Same Sky MD-S series datasheet dated 09/12/2024, page 3, MD-60S Recommended PCB Layout / Top View / Date Codes after 03/03/2022, https://www.sameskydevices.com/product/resource/md-s.pdf : 6 x 0.9 +0.1/-0 mm dia holes, row 3/1/2/4 at 8.50 mm and row 5/6 at 11.00 mm from the mating face (X MIRRORED from the datasheet drawing: the Same Sky layout is drawn with the mating face at the BOTTOM of the page, i.e. rotated 180 deg from this footprint's face-at-y=0 orientation, which also reverses left/right. Sanity rule for this footprint (mating face at y=0, body at +y): an observer facing the socket sees left-to-right = DECREASING x, so the front view reads 6(+3.4) 5(-3.4) upper, 4(+3.4) 3(-3.4) middle, 2(+1.3) 1(-1.3) lower - the standard PS/2 female socket front view, which is the mirror of the plug), outer columns 6.80 mm apart and the inner pair 2.60 mm apart, earth-terminal slot 2.2 x 0.7 mm on the centreline 4.70 mm from the face, body 14.0 x 12.4 x 12.8 mm. Cross-checked against Kycon KMDGX-xS-N rev B5 (03/28/18) 6-position Recommended PCB Layout (Bottom View), https://www.kycon.com/Pub_Eng_Draw/KMDGX-xS-N.pdf , which gives the same grid with 1.10 mm dia holes and a 2.30 mm dia locating boss in place of the earth tab (Kycon grid numbers map to standard pins as 1=1 2=2 3=3 5=4 6=5 8=6). Holes are drilled 1.10 mm and the centre feature is one plated 2.50 mm hole (pad SH) that clears both the CUI earth tab and the Kycon boss. 2.50 mm rather than the 2.40 mm first drawn: 2.40 leaves the Kycon 2.30 mm boss only 0.10 mm diametral slack, which becomes a press fit once plating thickness and hole tolerance are taken off, and the CUI 2.2 x 0.7 mm tab does not care either way. 3.20 mm pad keeps a 0.35 mm annular ring. Anchor (0,0) = centre of the mating face plane - place it on the board edge line. VERIFY AGAINST A PHYSICAL SAMPLE BEFORE FAB.")
		(tags "connector mini-din minidin md-60s kmdgx ps2 ps/2 6-pin socket receptacle right-angle tht amiga keyboard a4000 amigahid rev7")
